# AudioStream — Implementation Plan

## Goal
Transform the open-source [audio-share v0.3.4] codebase into **AudioStream** — a full-featured, bidirectional audio streaming solution between Windows PC and Android phone over USB tethering (and Wi-Fi), with:

- **PC → Phone**: Stream system audio to phone speakers
- **Phone → PC**: Stream phone microphone to PC as a virtual mic input (on-demand, no green dot until a PC app requests the mic)
- **Opus + PCM codec support** for low-latency compressed and lossless uncompressed streaming
- **Zero-setup auto-connection** when USB tethering is plugged in
- **Dear ImGui system tray app** on PC (dark gaming aesthetic, minimal resources)
- **Modified Jetpack Compose Android app** with full settings control

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Virtual Audio Driver Dependency**: We will bundle [VB-CABLE](https://vb-audio.com/Cable/) (freeware) as the virtual mic device. The installer will check if it's present and prompt installation if missing. VB-CABLE is widely trusted and used by millions. Alternative: we can also support [Virtual Audio Cable](https://vac.muzychenko.net/) if the user already has it.

> [!WARNING]  
> **EV Code Signing**: The compiled PC executable and any bundled driver installer will trigger Windows SmartScreen warnings unless signed with an EV code signing certificate. For personal use this is fine — just click "Run anyway". For distribution, a certificate would be needed (~$200-400/year).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Android RECORD_AUDIO Permission**: The modified Android app will request `RECORD_AUDIO` permission. Android 12+ shows the green privacy indicator when mic is actively recording. Our on-demand approach means this indicator only appears when a PC app is actually using the virtual mic.

