## Proposed Changes

### Component 1: Protocol Extension (Bidirectional + Codec Negotiation)

The existing protocol supports only PC→Phone PCM streaming. We need to extend it for bidirectional communication and codec negotiation.

#### [MODIFY] `protos/client.proto`

Add new message types for codec negotiation, mic stream control, and bidirectional audio:

```diff
+ // Codec types
+ enum AudioCodec {
+   CODEC_PCM = 0;      // Raw PCM (existing behavior)
+   CODEC_OPUS = 1;     // Opus compressed audio
+ }
+
+ // Extended audio format with codec info
+ message StreamConfig {
+   AudioFormat format = 1;       // Sample rate, channels, encoding
+   AudioCodec codec = 2;         // Codec selection
+   int32 opus_bitrate = 3;       // Opus bitrate (bps), 0 = auto
+   int32 opus_frame_size_ms = 4; // Opus frame duration: 5, 10, 20 ms
+ }
+
+ // Mic stream control
+ message MicControl {
+   bool start = 1;               // true = start mic capture, false = stop
+   StreamConfig config = 2;      // Desired mic stream format
+ }
+
  // Existing AudioFormat stays unchanged
```

#### [MODIFY] `server-core/src/network_manager.cpp`

Extend the command protocol:

```cpp
// Existing commands
CMD_GET_FORMAT    = 1,  // Client requests audio format
CMD_START_PLAY    = 2,  // Client starts playback session
CMD_HEARTBEAT     = 3,  // Keep-alive ping

// New commands
CMD_NEGOTIATE_CODEC = 4,  // Codec negotiation (Opus/PCM, bitrate, frame size)
CMD_START_MIC       = 5,  // PC requests phone to start mic capture
CMD_STOP_MIC        = 6,  // PC requests phone to stop mic capture
CMD_MIC_DATA        = 7,  // Mic audio data (phone → PC, over UDP)
CMD_DISCOVERY       = 8,  // UDP broadcast discovery beacon
CMD_ENCRYPTION_HANDSHAKE = 9,  // Optional TLS/DTLS negotiation
```

**UDP Packet Header** (new, replaces raw PCM bytes):
```
[uint8  packet_type]     // 0x01 = PC audio, 0x02 = Mic audio
[uint16 sequence_num]    // For ordering & loss detection
[uint32 timestamp]       // RTP-style timestamp for jitter buffer
[bytes  payload]         // Opus frame or PCM data
```

