### Component 4: Virtual Mic On-Demand Detection

#### [NEW] `server-core/src/virtual_mic_monitor.h` / `.cpp`

Monitors whether any Windows application is reading from the VB-CABLE Output device (i.e., a VoIP app opened the virtual mic). When detected, signals the phone to start mic capture.

```cpp
class VirtualMicMonitor {
public:
    VirtualMicMonitor(asio::io_context& io);
    
    // Poll WASAPI session manager to detect active audio sessions
    // on the VB-CABLE Output device
    asio::awaitable<void> monitor_loop(
        std::function<void(bool)> on_state_change);  // true=active, false=inactive
    
private:
    // Uses IAudioSessionManager2 + IAudioSessionEnumerator
    // to detect when apps open the VB-CABLE Output recording device
    bool is_virtual_mic_in_use();
    
    std::string vb_cable_device_id_;
    bool last_state_ = false;
};
```

**Detection approach**: Use `IMMDeviceEnumerator` to find the VB-CABLE Output endpoint, then use `IAudioMeterInformation` or `IAudioSessionManager2` to detect when another process activates a capture session on it. Poll every 100ms (negligible CPU cost).

