### Component 6: Adaptive Jitter Buffer

#### [NEW] `server-core/src/audio/jitter_buffer.h` / `.cpp`

```cpp
class AdaptiveJitterBuffer {
public:
    enum Preset { LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, CUSTOM };
    
    AdaptiveJitterBuffer(int sample_rate, int channels, 
                         Preset preset = LOW);
    
    // Push received packet (may arrive out of order)
    void push(uint16_t seq, uint32_t timestamp, 
              const uint8_t* data, int len);
    
    // Pull next audio frame for playback (called by render thread)
    // Returns true if data available, false if underrun
    bool pull(float* pcm_output, int frame_size);
    
    // Statistics
    struct Stats {
        float avg_latency_ms;
        float jitter_ms;
        int packets_lost;
        int buffer_depth_ms;
        int underruns;
        int overruns;
    };
    Stats get_stats() const;
    
    void set_preset(Preset p);
    void set_custom_buffer_ms(int min_ms, int max_ms);
    
private:
    // Ring buffer of timestamped packets, sorted by sequence number
    // Adaptive target depth based on measured jitter
    struct Packet {
        uint16_t seq;
        uint32_t timestamp;
        std::vector<uint8_t> data;
    };
    std::map<uint16_t, Packet> buffer_;
    int target_depth_ms_;
    // ... statistics tracking
};
```

**Preset values**:
- **LOW**: 20ms target buffer (USB tethering)
- **MEDIUM**: 50ms target buffer (good Wi-Fi)
- **HIGH**: 100ms target buffer (unstable network)
- **CUSTOM**: User-defined min/max in ms

