### Component 10: Optional Encryption

#### TLS for TCP Control Channel

Using OpenSSL (already available via vcpkg):

```cpp
// Wrap TCP socket with asio::ssl::stream when encryption enabled
if (encryption_enabled_) {
    ssl::context ctx(ssl::context::tlsv13_client);
    ssl::stream<tcp::socket> secure_socket(std::move(socket), ctx);
    co_await secure_socket.async_handshake(ssl::stream_base::server, 
                                            asio::use_awaitable);
    // Use secure_socket for all control commands
}
```

For UDP audio: no encryption (USB tethering is physically secure; Wi-Fi encryption is handled at the WPA layer). User can enable DTLS in settings for additional security if desired.

